    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Thanks. One thing that's tripping me up is the sensor data from the last dive. We're seeing some really erratic, sudden spikes in the salinity readings that don't seem to correlate with the temperature changes or the local depth profile. It looks like noise, but it's almost too consistent to be simple sensor drift. Any idea what might cause those kinds of sudden, non-linear fluctuations in such a stable environment?",
