      "content": "Those types of fluctuations might be caused by unwanted signals or disturbances that are not directly related to the marine environment. External sources like seismic activity, ship traffic, or submersible intervention could generate vibrations that reach your sensors, leading to physical excursions that transfer into the moored enclosure. Alternatively, issues with the sedimentation dynamics or turbulence beneath the moored tether might also introduce undulations in the salinity signal that appear as non-linear fluctuations.",
